  "notes": "Phone and camera videos now open on a Mac without installing anything: H.264, HEVC and AAC go through the codecs that ship with macOS, and H.264/HEVC exports (including 10-bit HDR HEVC) are written by the system encoder into MP4. An FFmpeg found on this computer is used automatically for the formats macOS cannot read. Also fixes a crash when opening a file with LocalSR while it was not running.",
